      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #36, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ ⎕AV omitted the Member/Enlist symbol ∊ (U+220A) entirely, one of
      ⍝ the APL2 primitive characters apl2lrm.txt p.273/Appendix A says
      ⍝ must be present -- GNU APL's own primary glyph for this primitive
      ⍝ is ϵ (U+03F5, still unchanged below), but ∊ must also be
      ⍝ representable. Took over the ⎕AV slot vacated by demoting the
      ⍝ unused legacy IBM filler character DIAMOND_UNDERBAR (⍚).
      ⍝
      ⍴⎕AV
256

      '∊'∊⎕AV
1

      'ϵ'∊⎕AV
1

